From dab4672e165ab1d854c2546899f519e837c7653c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Schreiber <deezns@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:42:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Expose the client's SO_PEERCRED to NSS modules

nsncd performs every lookup in its own process, so an NSS module that
identifies its caller (through SO_PEERCRED on a socket it opens, or
getuid()) sees nsncd rather than the process that asked.

Record the client's SO_PEERCRED in a thread-local for the duration of
each request and export it from the binary as nsncd_peer_cred(), a C
function an NSS module can find with dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, ...) and call
from the thread performing the lookup.
---
